 "final_message": "All 11 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests).\n\n- **`metrics.py`**:\n  - `monitor_flag_rate` returns `0.0` for an empty list and counts only `True` as flagged, so `None` and `False` don't count.\n  - `pooled_flag_rate` now pools all transcripts across groups instead of averaging group rates.\n  - `flags_in_window` sums the last `days` entries, and `days == 0` gives `0`. Previously it summed `days + 1` entries.\n- **`loader.py`**:\n  - `parse_transcript_log` skips blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines, and strips whitespace around each field. It reads `flagged` as `1` \u2192 True, `0` \u2192 False, and empty \u2192 None.\n  - `dedupe_transcripts` keeps the last transcript for each id.\n  - `daily_flag_counts` returns one entry per day from `start_day` to `end_day` inclusive, with `0` for empty days. It returns `[]` when `end_day < start_day`.\n- **`report.py`**: `monitor_summary` rounds `rate` to 3 decimals and counts only groups that have at least one transcript.\n- **Tests**: I added one test for the `None` rule in `monitor_flag_rate` and one for keeping the last duplicate id in `dedupe_transcripts`.\n- **README**: the `flags_in_window` entry now describes the last `days` entries, and there is a new `daily_flag_counts` entry.\n\nI didn't add tests for the other spec rules I changed.",
